@page "/privacy"

<PageTitle>Privacy · RioCharts for Blazor and .NET</PageTitle>

<h1>Privacy</h1>
<p class="lead">
    This site has no accounts, no forms and no ads. It uses Microsoft Clarity to see how the documentation is used,
    so we can make it better. This page says what that means.
</p>

<h2>Usage statistics (Microsoft Clarity)</h2>
<p>
    On riocharts.com, <a href="https://clarity.microsoft.com">Microsoft Clarity</a> records how pages are used: which pages
    are opened, clicks, scrolling and mouse movement, the browser, device and screen size, and the approximate country.
    Text on the page is masked, and nothing you type is recorded. We use it only to see which pages help and where people
    get stuck.
</p>
<p>
    When you open <strong>Your data</strong> in the <a href="definitions">playground</a>, Clarity stops for the rest of your
    visit, before you pick a file. Your data is read in your browser and is never sent anywhere.
</p>
<p>
    Clarity runs without cookies here, so it cannot recognize you on a later visit. The data is processed by Microsoft;
    see the <a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement">Microsoft Privacy Statement</a>. To opt out, block
    <code>clarity.ms</code> with a content blocker or turn on your browser's tracking protection; the site works the same
    without it.
</p>

<h2>Other services</h2>
<ul>
    <li>The site is hosted on <a href="https://docs.github.com/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub Pages</a>, which may log your IP address for security.</li>
    <li>Fonts load from <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google Fonts</a>, which sees your IP address when your browser fetches them.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Stored in your browser</h2>
<p>
    If you switch between light and dark mode, the choice is kept in your browser's local storage
    (<code>rio-docs-theme</code>). It never leaves your device.
</p>

<h2>Questions</h2>
<p>
    Open an <a href="https://github.com/joadan/RioCharts/issues">issue on GitHub</a>.
</p>
